Interesting, or if I've got nested time data (like month and year) could I do -

s( lat , long , month/year ) ?

The only reservation I have is that lat and long are meant to be a 2-dimensional isotropic smooth, so should time be part of that or in a different smoothing function?

I could decompose time into days -- it's 6 full years of data, but I could just count from day 1 through day n and make it a single integer for time.

How could I narrow down to individual slices of time with this approach? Say I wanted a sequence of maps or an animation showing how odds vary over lat/long over time, can that be pulled out of a smooth like that?

